PREREQUISITES:
1. Install PuTTY from putty.org.
2. AWS account with 2 EC2 instances (Ubuntu/Debian recommended).
3. Key pairs (.pem) converted to .ppk using PuTTYgen if needed.
4. Security group: Allow All TCP from Anywhere for testing.

INSTANCE SETUP:
Launch 2 instances with:
   a.Choose Ubuntu Server 22.04 in Application and OS Images (Amazon Machine Image).
   b.Choose t3.small in Instance Type.
   c.Create a keypair using .pem.
   d.Add All TCP and ANYWHERE in the network ip in the Security group.
   e.Change their names to slave and master.

MASTER NODE CONFIGURATION:
1.Update & Install Dependencies:
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install wget
2.Update Hosts File:
  sudo nano /etc/hosts
  # Add:
  <private_ip_of_master> puppet
3.Install Puppet Master:
  wget https://apt.puppetlabs.com/puppet-release-bionic.deb
  sudo dpkg -i puppet-release-bionic.deb
  sudo apt-get install puppet-master
4.Verify & Configure:
  apt policy puppet-master
  sudo systemctl status puppet-master.service
  sudo vim /etc/default/puppet-master #You can also use nano and if it appears empty just add it.
  # Add/modify JAVA_ARGS
  JAVA_ARGS="-Xms512m -Xmx512m"
  sudo systemctl restart puppet-master.service
  sudo ufw allow 8140/tcp   # Open communication port
---MASTER SET-UP COMPLETE---

SLAVE NODE CONFIGURATION:
1.Update $ Install Puppet:
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install wget
2.Update Hosts File:
  sudo nano /etc/hosts
  # Add:
  <private_ip_of_master> puppet
3.Install Puppet Master:
  wget https://apt.puppetlabs.com/puppet-release-bionic.deb
  sudo dpkg -i puppet-release-bionic.deb
  sudo apt-get install puppet
  sudo systemctl start puppet
  sudo systemctl enable puppet
---SLAVE SET-UP COMPLETE---

MASTER-SLAVE CERTIFICATE SIGNING:
On Master:
  sudo puppet cert list --all
  sudo puppet cert sign --all

CREATING FIRST MANIFEST:
1.Create Manifest Directory:
  sudo mkdir -p /etc/puppet/code/environments/production/manifests/
  sudo nano /etc/puppet/code/environments/production/manifests/site.pp
  Add:
      file { '/tmp/puppet_test.txt':
      ensure  => present,
      mode    => '0644',
      content => "Working on ${ipaddress_eth0}!\n",
      }
2.Restart Puppet Master:
  sudo systemctl restart puppet-master

APPLY MANIFEST ON SLAVE:
cd /tmp
ls   # check the files
sudo puppet agent --test
cat puppet_test.txt  # verify the content

INSTALLING & CONFIGURING NGINX VIA PUPPET:
1.MASTER: Create new_site.pp:
  sudo nano /etc/puppet/code/environments/production/manifests/new_site.pp
2.Manifest Content:
  node default {
  # Install nginx
  package { 'nginx':
    ensure => installed,
  }

  # Ensure nginx service is running
  service { 'nginx':
    ensure => running,
  }

  # Create index.html
  file { '/var/www/html/index.html':
    ensure  => present,
    mode    => '0644',
    content => "Welcome All by DevOps Domain - KD17",
  }

  # Optional: create status file
  file { '/tmp/status.txt':
    content => 'Nginx has been installed successfully',
    mode    => '0644',
  }
}

2.SLAVE: Apply Manifest:
  sudo puppet agent --test
3.VERIFICATIOn:
  a.Open web browser → http://<slave_public_ip> → should show the custom page.
  b.Check status file:
    cat /tmp/status.txt

-----SET-UP COMPLETE-----
